<title>UK: Southern Newspapers to cut workforce.</title>
<headline>Southern Newspapers to cut workforce.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern Newspapers said on Thursday it planned to cut its workforce by 10 to 15 percent over a two-year period as part of the reorganisation of its newspaper publishing and printing operations.</p>
<p>The company said the job losses would affect 130-200 posts across all departments and include 35 voluntary redundancies.  </p>
<p>The company said it would immediately merge its central and eastern regions into a single southern region.</p>
<p>In April, the company's eastern Region publishing operations moved from the centre of Southampton to a new 35 million stg publishing and printing centre on the outskirts of the city.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
